00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:54.920
Researchers at Bite Dance, with co-authors at Princeton, Stanford, and the University of California, Berkeley,

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:59.780
found that memory compression methods in deep-seek artificial intelligence, or AI,

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:05.020
models can raise the chance of a miss depending on where information sits in a long input.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:11.800
the South China Morning Post reports. The paper is not yet peer-reviewed. The tests use deep-seek V4

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:16.800
and compressed variants of it. The coverage treats this as an uncommon outside look at the

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:22.640
cost-cutting method that helped the Chinese lab close in on US competitors open AI and anthropic.

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:28.960
The same method that lowers memory use may also cut reliability on some jobs. Code-related queries

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:34.400
were an example, especially when irrelevant text came before the useful material. Developers and

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:38.420
users will now test whether newer versions ease that sensitivity to position.

