00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:04.820
To really understand why a cheaper model can skip a fact that is already in its input,

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:09.820
you have to look at how memory compression works inside a large language model, the kind

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:12.960
of system that writes text and code from a huge training set.

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:18.040
A lot of talk about efficient models stops at lower training bills and cheaper running costs.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:21.340
It often skips the machinery that produces those savings.

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:26.480
These systems cut memory by squeezing how they store and fetch information across a long

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:27.960
stretch of text or code.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:31.880
That squeeze can shorten the effective context window in some positions.

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:35.240
The span of material the model can actually keep in play.

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:40.700
When that happens, the model is more likely to overlook a detail in those spots or to give

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:41.560
it the wrong weight.

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:44.620
The pattern is not the property of a single laboratory.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:49.420
It shows up whenever designers trade storage capacity for speed or for cost.

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:54.700
So when a cheaper model is said to match frontier performance, the useful check is whether

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:58.480
the tests included long-context work, or only short prompts.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:03.820
Ask whether the model was tried on inputs longer than a few thousand tokens, the small

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:08.600
chunks of text it reads, and whether accuracy stayed level when the important detail was

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:10.300
moved around inside those inputs.

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:13.860
Primary technical reports often show those trade-offs.

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:15.900
Press summaries often do not.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:22.080
South China Morning Post treated the latest AI news as a reliability cost inside cheaper models,

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:26.900
while Reuters treated the same boom as a profit wave at the factory that makes the chips.

